  "complexity": 5,
  "title": "R5: orchestrator/sched_scorecard.py \u2014 scheduling scorecard: predicted vs actual interference, stale outcomes, duration error, queue time and heuristic validation (AP P14)",
  "spec": "Why: waves.jsonl records predicted interference and priorities (daemon.dispatch wave_row: ready, running, baseline_order, wave, deferred, predicted [{a,b,level,reasons}], priority {tid: critical_path.explain}, applied), stale.jsonl records stale checks, dispatch.jsonl records skip reasons, and merge.merge fails tasks with reason rebase_conflict \u2014 but nothing joins predictions to outcomes, so the heuristics are unvalidated (AP P14; brief P9).\nWhat: new pure module orchestrator/sched_scorecard.py reading via schedlog.read_with_malformed and the tasks dir under root; no daemon edits.\n- pair_outcomes(root) -> rows per predicted pair {a, b, level, predicted_reasons, both_ran_concurrently (both dispatched before either gated), actual_conflict (either task later reason rebase_conflict / hold merge conflict / stale row action rebase_conflict), stale_event (stale row risk high for either), fix_round (any fix-round child via constraints.fix_round_for), serialized (pair appeared in deferred with hard:/soft: reason)}.\n- task_outcomes(root) -> per execute task {queue_wait_s (dispatched_at - first_ready_at or created), predicted_duration_s (from the latest waves row priority[tid].est_duration_s), actual_duration_s (duration.actual_s), error (duration.prediction_error), critical_path_s (priority), accepted (merged_into set), fix_rounds, total_tokens/usd from runs rows for the task lineage when present}.\n- build(root=STATE) -> card {\"hard_conflict_precision\": conflicts among concurrently-run hard-predicted pairs / such pairs or None, \"soft_conflict_usefulness\": conflict rate of concurrently-run soft pairs vs none-level pairs, \"unnecessary_serialization\": serialized pairs whose tasks' changed files (task.changed_files or scope literals) were disjoint / serialized pairs, \"conflict_rate\", \"stale_work_rate\", \"duration_mape\" and n, \"median_queue_wait_s\", \"goal_latency_s\" per goal from tasks (min created to max merged), \"accepted_cost_usd\" sum, \"n_waves\", \"n_pairs\", \"malformed\"}; None for undefined metrics, never a fabricated 0.\n- format(card) -> text table; every metric line shows n.\nDepends on R1 duration.actual_s/prediction_error (import orchestrator.duration).",
  "inputs": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_sched_scorecard.py::test_predicted_hard_pair_that_conflicted_counts_toward_precision \u2014 a waves row predicting hard for (A,B), both dispatched concurrently, B later failed rebase_conflict: hard_conflict_precision 1.0 with n 1",
    "tests/test_sched_scorecard.py::test_stale_outcomes_are_attributed_to_pairs_and_rate \u2014 stale rows with risk high for a predicted pair set stale_event True and stale_work_rate reflects it",
    "tests/test_sched_scorecard.py::test_duration_prediction_error_uses_priority_estimate_and_actual \u2014 predicted 1200 s, actual 600 s yields per-task error ratio 2.0 and duration_mape over tasks with both values",
    "tests/test_sched_scorecard.py::test_malformed_telemetry_is_tolerated_and_counted \u2014 broken lines in waves.jsonl and stale.jsonl are skipped, card.malformed counts them, undefined metrics are None not 0",
    "tests/test_sched_scorecard.py::test_unnecessary_serialization_detects_disjoint_deferred_pairs \u2014 a soft-deferred pair whose changed files were disjoint counts as unnecessary serialization 1.0"
  ],
  "scope": [
    "orchestrator/sched_scorecard.py",
    "tests/test_sched_scorecard.py"
  ],
